Chapter: MutableDefSeq
  cites Codex chapter General

 A function body may be several statements: each in-place field
 assignment runs, then the final expression is the result. Regression
 for a def body that once silently kept only the first statement, so a
 second assignment was dropped.

Section: Definitions

  mutable Box = record {
    n : Integer,
    m : Integer
  }

  bump-both : mutable Box -> mutable Box
  bump-both (b) =
    b.n = b.n + 1
    b.m = b.m + 10
    b

  show-box : mutable Box -> Text
  show-box (b) = "n=" & show (b.n) & " m=" & show (b.m)

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (show-box (bump-both (Box { n = 0, m = 0 })))
  end
